---
/* CraftiPlays / Lands of Magic project page.  URL: /portfolio/craftiplays
   Images go in public/portfolio/craftiplays/ */
import ProjectPage from '../../layouts/ProjectPage.astro';

// Building blocks for the part below the description
import FeatureImage from '../../components/project/FeatureImage.astro';
import BigSmall from '../../components/project/BigSmall.astro';
import Statement from '../../components/project/Statement.astro';
import UnevenPair from '../../components/project/UnevenPair.astro';
import MyPart from '../../components/project/MyPart.astro';
import CompareSlider from '../../components/project/CompareSlider.astro';
---


<ProjectPage
  pageTitle="Lands of Magic — Game Assets — Paulina Cywoniuk"
  pageDescription="Illustrated game assets for the mobile game 'Lands of Magic' by CraftiPlays."

  logo="/portfolio/craftiplays/craftiplays-logo.png"
  logoAlt="CraftiPlays logo"

  title={'Lands of Magic'}
  subtitle="Mobile Game Assets Design"

  headerImage="/portfolio/craftiplays/craftiplays-header.png"
  headerAlt="Colourful illustrated game assets for Lands of Magic"

  accent="var(--color-cyan)"
  accentText="var(--color-purple)"

  keywords={["Mobile Game", "Unity + Adobe Suite", "Team", "10 months"]}
>

  <p>
    In 2021 I was part of a team at CraftiPlays, who hired me as a graphic designer for
    their ongoing project — a mobile game called <em>Lands of Magic</em>. My role
    consisted of making illustrations of assets for the game that were consistent with
    the style of an asset pack they had already purchased before I joined the team.
  </p>
  <p>
    All designs I made for them are vectorised in Illustrator, so that the whole team
    can use them according to their needs. In <em>Lands of Magic</em>, the illustrations
    became more than just functional assets; they played a role in immersing players in
    a magical world where visuals enrich the storytelling and gameplay experience.
  </p>

  <Fragment slot="sections">

    <FeatureImage
      src="/portfolio/craftiplays/LandsOfMagic-Vizualization.jpg"
      alt="Illustrated cauldron and magical houses in seasonal versions"
      caption="Mobile game Lands of Magic - UI elements and illustrated assets for the magical world."
    />

    <BigSmall
      bigSrc="/portfolio/craftiplays/craftiplays-trees-development.jpg"
      bigAlt="Illustrated magical plants and trees"
            bigAlt="Illustrated magical plants and trees"
      bigFit="contain"
            smallSrc="/portfolio/craftiplays/craftiplays-gui-pack.jpg"
            bigCaption="Study of the shapes to create flora assets."
      smallAlt="Preview of the GUI asset pack The Stone, the style my illustrations had to match"
      smallHref="https://assetstore.unity.com/packages/2d/gui/gui-the-stone-116852"
      smallCredit="Asset pack: GUI The Stone (not my work)"
      smallCaption="Original asset pack that I had to match."
      heading="Matching an existing style"
    >
      Every new asset design had to fit the style of an asset pack the team had already bought before I joined.
    </BigSmall>

    <Statement>
      I was tasked to design, in matching to existing style, assets that would reflect the magical and cartoonish style of the in-game world.
    </Statement>

    <UnevenPair
      aSrc="/portfolio/craftiplays/craftiplays-currencies-background.jpg"
      aAlt="In-game currency in illustrated environment plus loading bar UI"
      aCaption="In-game currencies in illustrated environment with loading bar UI."
      bSrc="/portfolio/craftiplays/green-eye-process.jpg"
      bAlt="Process of designing the Green Eye event currency"
      bCaption="Process of designing the Green Eye event currency."
    />

    <MyPart heading="Seasonal skins">
      <!-- Two sliders, one per building. The wrapper takes the
           "main" spot of MyPart, so both sit where its big image would. -->
      <div slot="main" class="skin-sliders">
        <figure class="skin-slider">
          <CompareSlider
            beforeSrc="/portfolio/craftiplays/craftiplays-shop-normal.jpg"
            beforeAlt="Witch Shop building in its normal skin"
            beforeLabel="Normal"
            afterSrc="/portfolio/craftiplays/craftiplays-shop-halloween.jpg"
            afterAlt="Witch Shop building in its Halloween skin"
            afterLabel="Halloween"
          />
          <figcaption>Witch Shop: normal and Halloween skin.</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <figure class="skin-slider">
          <CompareSlider
            beforeSrc="/portfolio/craftiplays/craftiplays-lake-normal.jpg"
            beforeAlt="Golden Lake building in its normal skin"
            beforeLabel="Normal"
            afterSrc="/portfolio/craftiplays/craftiplays-lake-summer.jpg"
            afterAlt="Golden Lake building in its summer skin"
            afterLabel="Summer"
          />
          <figcaption>Golden Lake: normal and summer skin.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>

      <p> Additionally to creating assets that match the existing style, I was able to design skins for various in game events. The seasonal skins allowed us to give the game world a fresh look for each event while maintaining consistency with the overall art direction.</p>
    </MyPart>

  </Fragment>

</ProjectPage>
<style>
  /* The two seasonal-skin sliders, stacked */
  .skin-sliders {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: clamp(3.5rem, 8vw, 6rem);        /* KNOB: space between the two sliders */
  }

  .skin-slider {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .skin-slider figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;                  /* KNOB: space between slider and its caption */
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
</style>